{
  "about": "The built-in types of class diagrams. A class's text keeps neutral UML types (`name` and `aliases`); `in` is how each language writes them (in the order of `languages`), `read` is what may be picked or typed per language and the neutral type it means, in the order the type picker shows them. `cases` are checked by codegen/types.rs (neutral to language) and src/lib/classTypes.test.ts (both ways). Used by crates/flow-core/src/codegen/types.rs and src/lib/classTypes.ts.",
